{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the soul of the people grew impatient</b> — teaches that they saw all the troubles that would come upon them in the exile of Edom, and how the exile would drag on." "<b>ותקצר</b> — Four times in the Masorah: ותקצר נפש העם, ותקצר נפשו בעמל ישראל, ותקצר נפשו למות, ותקצר נפשי בהם. Since they came to the border of Edom — ותקצר נפש העם וידברו בה' ובמשה — and ותקצר נפשו בעמל ישראל: they sinned. ותקצר נפשו למות: Aaron died at the border of Edom. And likewise ותקצר נפשי בהם at the beginning of the verse. And I will cut off three shepherds in one month — which they expounded upon Aaron, Miriam, and Moses, who all three died in one month."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "The four Masorah citations are drawn from Numbers 21:4, Judges 10:16, Job 3:21, and Ezekiel 21:20 respectively. The final phrase 'אכחיד ג׳ הרועים בירח אחד' quotes Zechariah 11:8. The phrase 'דרישא דקרא' (at the beginning of the verse) appears to signal that the fourth occurrence is the one under commentary."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:45.754088136Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}